The ORB runtime in crates/llmlip/src/orb_v3_omol.rs follows implementations
published by Orbital Materials in orb-models, v0.6.2, commit
 a5f1a382a72126feff0594b19891e03cde5f843e
https://github.com/orbital-materials/orb-models

Relevant upstream sources:
 orb_models/common/models/gns.py (Encoder, AttentionInteractionNetwork)
 orb_models/common/models/nn_util.py (ChargeSpinEmbedding, get_cutoff)
 orb_models/common/models/rbf.py (radial feature conventions)
 orb_models/forcefield/models (conservative energy model interfaces)

The Rust runtime is an altered implementation: fixed-weight storage and validation,
explicit input derivatives, fused attention, CPU parallelism and BLAS operations
replace the Python/PyTorch execution. It is not the upstream package and is not
endorsed by its authors. The ORB runtime module is distributed under Apache-2.0;
see LICENSE-APACHE and licenses/reference/orb.txt. Original contributions elsewhere
retain their stated MIT OR Apache-2.0 choice, subject to other retained notices.

